.TH MURALCTL 1 "August 22, 2026" "mural 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
muralctl \- control the mural wallpaper daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B muralctl
.RB [ --socket
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ --timeout-ms
.IR MS ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B muralctl
sends one JSON request to
.BR murald (1)
and prints the response. Native wallpaper commands operate on murald's
persistent wallpaper library and current layout state.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --socket " PATH"
Connect to PATH instead of the default mural socket.
.TP
.BI --timeout-ms " MS"
Give up if the daemon does not respond within MS milliseconds. The default is
30000.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Print the Mural version and exit without contacting the daemon.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ping
Check daemon health.
.TP
.B capabilities [--json]
Print the running daemon's protocol version and compiled-in transition
capabilities. The default is human-readable text;
.B --json
prints the versioned capability payload for scripts.
.TP
.B health [--json]
Print supervisor and renderer health as JSON, including renderer pid,
generation, restart count, last renderer error, diagnostic path, and per-output
renderability state.
.TP
.B query [--json]
Print daemon output state as JSON.
.TP
.BI set " --output NAME PATH " [ OPTIONS ]
Set explicit image paths for one or more outputs. May also use
.BI --output NAME=PATH .
.TP
.BI preload " --output NAME PATH"
Validate explicit image paths. Use
.B cache warm
to warm canvas thumbnails.
.TP
.BI clear " [--output NAME ...] [--color #RRGGBB]"
Clear selected outputs, or all known outputs, to a solid color.
.TP
.B next
Show the next wallpaper set from murald's shuffle/history state.
.TP
.B back
Show the previous wallpaper set.
.TP
.BI shift " [forward|back]"
Rotate the current wallpaper set across outputs in layout order.
.TP
.B shift-forward
Alias for shifting forward.
.TP
.B shift-back
Alias for shifting backward.
.TP
.BI replace " INDEX"
Replace the current wallpaper at output index INDEX.
.TP
.BI quarantine " INDEX"
Move the current wallpaper at INDEX to the quarantine directory and replace it.
The misspelling
.B quarentine
is accepted for compatibility.
.TP
.BI favorite " INDEX"
Add the current wallpaper at INDEX to the favorites list. Favorites remain in
the normal library but are inserted into the shuffle bag multiple times
according to
.BR favorite_weight ,
so future random selections pick them more often. The current displayed
wallpaper does not change.
.TP
.BI unfavorite " INDEX"
Remove the current wallpaper at INDEX from the favorites list, returning it to
normal shuffle-bag weight. The current displayed wallpaper does not change.
.TP
.B favorites
List favorite wallpaper paths.
.TP
.B current
Show current wallpaper rows as index, output, favorite marker, and path.
.TP
.B rescan
Rescan the top-level wallpaper directory.
.TP
.BI cache " status [--json]"
Show canvas thumbnail cache status.
.TP
.BI cache " warm [--scope current|all] [--workers N] [--backend auto|vips|internal] [--json]"
Schedule nonblocking canvas thumbnail cache warming. The
.B auto
backend prefers
.BR vipsthumbnail
when available and falls back to the internal decoder.
.TP
.BI cache " clear [--json]"
Remove cached canvas thumbnails from disk and clear the daemon's in-memory
canvas thumbnail cache state.
.TP
.BI world " cache status [--json]"
Inspect the virtual world cache. This command runs offline and does
not require a running daemon. Status output includes the
.B path-snapshot-v1
order policy plus the last real compute failure count and failure log path.
.TP
.BI world " cache index [--json]"
Write or refresh the world cache manifest for the current top-level wallpaper
library. This indexes paths only; it does not generate image tiles yet.
.TP
.BI world " cache failures [--json]"
Print the current world-cache last-compute failure records directly. Plain
output is tab-separated
.IR kind ,
.IR item ,
and
.IR message .
JSON output includes the failure log path, count, and records.
.TP
.BI world " cache compute --scope all [--dry-run] [--background] [--limit N] [--tile-limit N] [--workers N] [--progress] [--json]"
Generate real per-wall cell thumbnails and the all-library world tile LOD
pyramid, or report planned work without writing image cache data when
.B --dry-run
is supplied. Plans and generated tile work report ready/missing counts with
LOD labels. Dry-run plans include an estimated remaining byte count. Real
compute runs rewrite the last-compute failure log and progress output ends
with elapsed time and work rate.
.B --background
starts a detached local compute process and prints the child PID plus a
cache-local log path.
.TP
.BI world " cache compute --scope route --from PATH --to PATH [--dry-run] [--background] [--tile-limit N] [--workers N] [--progress] [--json]"
.TQ
.BI world " cache compute --scope route --route FROM TO [--route FROM TO ...] [--dry-run] [--background] [--tile-limit N] [--workers N] [--progress] [--json]"
Generate only the selected bounded route LOD needed for the route rectangle
between one or more library path pairs. Selected LOD tiles are deduplicated
across route pairs and generated directly from real source imagery or existing
cell thumbnails without forcing persistent per-wall thumbnail generation for
the route scope. Plans and generated tile work report ready/missing counts with
LOD labels. Dry-run plans include an estimated remaining byte count. Real
compute runs rewrite the last-compute failure log and progress output ends with
elapsed time and work rate.
Undecodable source cells are left transparent in the generated route tile and
recorded in the last-compute failure log rather than blocking the whole tile.
.B --workers
parallelizes LOD tile child-block generation.
.B --background
starts a detached local compute process and prints the child PID plus a
cache-local log path.
.TP
.BI world " cache compute --scope neighborhood --center PATH [--center PATH ...] [--radius N] [--lod N] [--dry-run] [--background] [--tile-limit N] [--workers N] [--progress] [--json]"
Generate selected world tiles around one or more library paths. The default
radius of 0 warms only the tile containing each center path; larger radii add
neighboring tiles at the selected LOD. This is intended for current/target
neighborhood prefetch without warming the whole library. Plans and generated
tile work report ready/missing counts with LOD labels. Dry-run plans include an
estimated remaining byte count. Real compute runs rewrite the last-compute
failure log and progress output ends with elapsed time and work rate.
.B --background
starts a detached local compute process and prints the child PID plus a
cache-local log path.
.TP
.B stop
Ask murald to exit cleanly.
.SH WALLPAPER OPTIONS
The
.B set
command accepts
.BR cut ,
.BR fade ,
.BR world ,
and
.BR push: DIR
transitions. Wallpaper navigation commands
.BR next ,
.BR back ,
.BR shift ,
.BR replace ,
and
.B quarantine
accept these overrides:
.TP
.BI --transition " NAME"
One of
.BR cut ,
.BR fade ,
.BR push:up ,
.BR push:down ,
.BR push:left ,
.BR push:right ,
.BR canvas ,
.BR canvas:auto ,
.BR canvas:horizontal ,
.BR canvas:vertical ,
or the experimental
.BR world
transition.
.B canvas
is valid only for wallpaper navigation commands because it requires mural
history and shuffle state.
.B world
is valid for wallpaper navigation commands and explicit
.B set
requests when the current and target wallpapers are present in the ordered
library and the required real world cache tiles are ready.
.TP
.BI --duration-ms " MS"
Transition duration in milliseconds.
.TP
.BI --easing " NAME"
One of
.BR linear ,
.BR ease-out-cubic ,
or
.BR ease-in-out-cubic .
.TP
.BI --mode " NAME"
For push, one of
.BR portal ,
.BR screen ,
or
.BR pan .
For canvas, one of
.BR clipped ,
.BR morph ,
.BR overlap ,
.BR collage ,
or
.BR span .
Canvas
.B collage
and
.B span
require
.BR "--canvas-walk strip" .
.TP
.BI --canvas-zoom-out-ms " MS"
Select
.B canvas
and set the zoom-out phase.
.TP
.BI --canvas-pan-ms " MS"
Select
.B canvas
and set the overview pan phase.
.TP
.BI --canvas-zoom-in-ms " MS"
Select
.B canvas
and set the zoom-in phase.
.TP
.BI --canvas-pan-axis " auto|horizontal|vertical"
Select
.B canvas
and set the natural-order pan axis.
.TP
.BI --canvas-walk " paged|strip"
Select
.B canvas
and set the canvas walk order.
.B paged
walks the bounded canvas from top-left through rows/columns;
.B strip
uses the older centered infinite-right strip.
.TP
.BI --canvas-overview-scale " SCALE"
Select
.B canvas
and set the overview tile scale as a fraction of the output. Lower values zoom
farther out.
.TP
.BI --canvas-tile-count " auto|N"
Select
.B canvas
and set automatic tile count or an exact tile count.
.TP
.BI --canvas-max-tile-count " N"
Select
.B canvas
and cap automatic tile count. Maximum: 256.
.TP
.BI --scale-mode " NAME"
One of
.BR fill ,
.BR fit ,
.BR center ,
or
.BR stretch .
.TP
.B --json
Print the wallpaper response as JSON instead of text.
.SH OUTPUT
Most daemon-control commands print JSON. Wallpaper commands print
script-friendly text by default unless
.B --json
is supplied.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Request succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
CLI, connection, or transport error.
.TP
.B 2
The daemon returned an error response, or an offline status command found an
expected not-ready state.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR murald (1),
.BR mural-config (5)
